# Lifeblood speech: news and gossip. The format and every fact and word are described in basics.speech.
#
# Facts: news (dating, engagement, wedding, breakup, birth, death, killing, attack, brawl), exaggerated (yes when the
# story grew in the telling), firsthand (yes if the teller saw it or it's their family; only for the one telling it),
# subject_opinion and other_opinion (what the speaker thinks of those involved). Words: subject (who it's about),
# other (the other person), baby (a newborn's name), source (who told the teller, when it's second-hand).
# Built from beats like topics.speech: a lead-in, the news, and the speaker's take on it, the last optional.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Telling it

== chat_open_news ==
[listener]! [news_lead] [news_item] [news_take?]
[listener]. [news_item] [news_take?] {taciturn}

== news_tell ==
[news_lead] [news_item] [news_take?]
[news_item] [news_take?]     {taciturn, w=2}

== news_lead ==
Did you hear?
Have you heard?
You'll never guess.          {extrovert}
Oh, have I got news for you. {nosy, w=3}
Come here, come here.        {nosy, w=2}
Don't tell anyone I told you. {nosy, w=2}
I probably shouldn't say, but... {polite}
Big news.                    {lighthearted}
Not to gossip, but...        {humble}

== news_item ==
[subject] and [other] are courting. {news=dating, exaggerated=no}
[subject]'s been seeing [other]. {news=dating, exaggerated=no}
[subject] and [other] are courting. Can't keep their hands off each other, I hear. {news=dating, exaggerated=yes, w=3}
[subject] and [other] are engaged! {news=engagement, exaggerated=no}
[subject] asked [other] to marry them, and they said yes! {news=engagement, exaggerated=no}
[subject] and [other] are engaged. Got down on one knee in front of everyone, I hear. {news=engagement, exaggerated=yes, w=3}
[subject] and [other] got married! {news=wedding, exaggerated=no}
[subject] and [other] tied the knot. {news=wedding, exaggerated=no}
[subject] and [other] got married. Already expecting, too, if you ask me. {news=wedding, exaggerated=yes, w=3}
[subject] and [other] split up. {news=breakup, exaggerated=no}
It's over between [subject] and [other]. {news=breakup, exaggerated=no}
[subject] and [other] split up. Screaming at each other in the street, they were. {news=breakup, exaggerated=yes, w=3}
[subject] and [other] had a baby! [baby], they called it. {news=birth, exaggerated=no}
There's a new little one: [baby]. [subject] and [other]'s. {news=birth, exaggerated=no}
[subject] and [other] had a baby. Twins, almost! {news=birth, exaggerated=yes, w=3}
[subject] died.              {news=death, exaggerated=no}
We lost [subject].           {news=death, exaggerated=no}
[subject] passed.            {news=death, exaggerated=no, polite}
[subject] died. Nobody knows how, and nobody's saying. {news=death, exaggerated=yes, w=3}
[subject] killed [other].    {news=killing, exaggerated=no}
[other] is dead. [subject] did it. {news=killing, exaggerated=no}
[subject] killed [other]. In cold blood, they say. Laughed about it after. {news=killing, exaggerated=yes, w=3}
[subject] attacked [other]. Out of nowhere. {news=attack, exaggerated=no}
[subject] went for [other], for no reason at all. {news=attack, exaggerated=no}
[subject] nearly beat [other] to death! {news=attack, exaggerated=yes, w=3}
[subject] and [other] got into a scrap. [subject] won. {news=brawl, exaggerated=no}
[subject] beat [other] in a fistfight. {news=brawl, exaggerated=no}
[subject] knocked [other] out cold with one punch! {news=brawl, exaggerated=yes, w=3}

# The teller's take on it: how they found out, and what they think.
== news_take ==
I saw it myself.             {firsthand=yes, w=0.6}
I heard it from [source].    {firsthand=no, w=0.6}
[source] told me. So it must be true. {firsthand=no, liar, w=0.8}
[source] told me, so take it with a grain of salt. {firsthand=no, honest, w=0.8}
Good for them.               {news=dating}
Good for them.               {news=engagement}
Isn't it lovely?             {news=wedding, romantic, w=2}
Isn't it lovely?             {news=engagement, romantic, w=2}
About time, too.             {news=wedding}
Give it a year.              {news=wedding, pessimist, w=2}
Poor [other]. They could do better. {news=dating, subject_opinion=disliked, w=2}
Poor [other]. They could do better. {news=wedding, subject_opinion=disliked, w=2}
Can't say I'm surprised.     {news=breakup}
Poor [subject].              {news=breakup, subject_opinion=friend, w=2}
Poor [subject].              {news=breakup, subject_opinion=close_friend, w=2}
Good riddance, if you ask me. {news=breakup, other_opinion=disliked, rude, w=2}
Babies everywhere these days. {news=birth, lighthearted}
A new little one. Makes you hopeful. {news=birth, optimist}
The Cube God bless that child. {news=birth, pious, w=2}
They were a good one.        {news=death, subject_opinion=friend, w=2}
They were a good one.        {news=death, subject_opinion=close_friend, w=2}
Cube God rest them.          {news=death, pious, w=2}
It comes for us all.         {news=death, serious}
I'd keep away from [subject] if I were you. {news=killing}
Poor [other].                {news=killing}
Someone ought to do something about [subject]. {news=killing, brave, w=2}
Lock your doors tonight.     {news=killing, timid, w=2}
Cube God judge them.         {news=killing, pious, w=2}
Watch yourself around [subject]. {news=attack}
Doesn't surprise me one bit. {news=attack, subject_opinion=disliked, w=2}
Doesn't surprise me one bit. {news=attack, subject_opinion=enemy, w=2}
Poor [other]. Are they all right? {news=attack, polite}
Wish I'd seen it.            {news=brawl, extrovert}
Grown folk, fighting like children. {news=brawl, serious, w=2}
Serves [other] right.        {news=brawl, other_opinion=disliked, w=2}
I'd like to see [subject] try that with me. {news=brawl, competitive, w=2}

